Closed with reason: Superseded — do not run. The parent epic's 2026-11-01 vmcore evidence identified the mt7921e driver as the source directly, so the 7-day Ethernet-only isolation *experiment* has no remaining question to answer (its purpose was to implicate/exonerate the module; the vmcore implicates it with a stack trace). Absorbed rather than deleted:
  1. its blacklist procedure is the live mitigation, documented reversibly on WL-0MVYAZQEB006HBOP AC-2;
  2. its validation role is taken by WL-0MVYEQKAM003THSP (24 h durability check, due 2026-11-02 21:08) — 24 h is sufficient because the pre-mitigation MTBF was ~24 min, so a 7-day window would add no information;
  3. its evidence-analysis requirements are met by the forensics tooling (WL-0MVY898D4007BZ28, scripts/collect-freeze-evidence.sh).
Re-open only if new evidence re-opens the question of *which* subsystem takes the host down.
